# stranded-finalized allowlist (T-2833)
#
# Tasks that legitimately sit in .tasks/active/ declaring `status:
# work-completed` with no `date_finished`. One path per line — repo-relative
# (normal), absolute, or bare filename all match. A trailing `# reason` is
# required by convention: the reason IS the justification, and "it's fine" is
# not one.
#
# Entries are still COUNTED and REPORTED; they only stop the check firing.
# Removing a line re-fires that task. A NEW stranded task fires immediately
# because it is not listed.
#
# NOTE: T-193 partial-complete tasks do NOT belong here. They carry a real
# `date_finished` and are excluded by the detector itself, not by
# acknowledgement — 58 of them in this corpus. If you find yourself adding one,
# the discriminator has drifted and the script is what needs fixing.
#
# Currently empty on purpose. The two real instances (T-2831, T-2832) were
# REPAIRED, not acknowledged — an entry here is for a task that is correct as it
# stands, never for one whose finalize should have completed.
